REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 6294)
  AUTHORS   Kunceviciene,E., Sriubiene,M., Liutkeviciene,R., Miceikiene,I.T.
            and Smalinskiene,A.
  TITLE     Heritability of myopia and its relation with GDJ2 and RASGRF1 genes
            in Lithuania
  JOURNAL   BMC Ophthalmol 18 (1), 124 (2018)
   PUBMED   29793445
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Our studies have shown that the heritability of myopia
            makes 66.4% in Lithuania. We detected significant associations
            between the combinations of GJD2 CC and RASGRF1 GT and odds ratio
            of developing myopia.
REFERENCE   4  (bases 1 to 6294)
  AUTHORS   Chen,H., Xu,Z., Yang,B., Zhou,X. and Kong,H.
  TITLE     RASGRF1 Hypermethylation, a Putative Biomarker of Colorectal Cancer
  JOURNAL   Ann Clin Lab Sci 48 (1), 3-10 (2018)
   PUBMED   29530990
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Low RASGRF1 expression due to hypermethylation is
            associated with Colorectal Cancer.
REFERENCE   5  (bases 1 to 6294)
  AUTHORS   Hepei,L., Mingkun,X., Li,W. and Jin,W.
  TITLE     Assessment of BicC family RNA binding protein 1 and Ras protein
            specific guanine nucleotide releasing factor 1 as candidate genes
            for high myopia: A case-control study
  JOURNAL   Indian J Ophthalmol 65 (10), 926-930 (2017)
   PUBMED   29044055
  REMARK    GeneRIF: genetic variants in BICC1 and RASGRF1 are closely
            associated with high myopia, which appears to be a potential
            candidate for high myopia in Chinese Han population.
